+# TB-SEC-KEY-01-R2A — dedicated local credential enrollment (scoped installed PASS)
+
+## Implementation
+The installed Settings → Account connections page displays presence-only values through the private dashboard backend and a separate Unix status-only vault socket. The status socket has a fixed request, exact desk peer UID, fixed validated response schema, and no enrollment, read, export or removal operations. The independent credential-operator account still exclusively owns write access to the separate enrollment socket. The prior development-only browser form remains compatible but is absent and its save handler refuses in installed mode; the gateway and backend independently deny browser enrollment.
+
+The dedicated local LightDM/X11 credential-operator session uses the existing strict logind caller, account, local display and active/unlocked session checks, validates a unique private local Xauthority cookie with no extra display grants, and uses the existing fail-closed session-event latch. A root-owned opt-in marker is required. Unlike recovery approval, it uses the operator's private home Xauthority directly; it does not copy it or access the independent recovery signing account. The fixed LightDM wrapper accepts either of two exact session entry paths, each enforcing the distinct account identity. The installed graphical window supports masked write-only Kraken read-only pair, Telegram Desk and Recovery token, and optional Grok key enrollment; explicit confirmation, paired replacement, local removal and status refresh. Inputs are cleared, copy/cut disabled, fixed failures, no plaintext status; no guarantee of in-process memory erasure. A lock/session change terminates the window; the UI guard does not assert transactional revocation of an already dispatched write. The trusted operator UID remains the enrollment principal; the previous local CLI is retained for administrative compatibility, not required for graphical operations. No changes to PAPER/live authorization, credentials never enable trading.
+
+**Deployment:** root-reviewed offline LightDM desktop requirements as previously qualified, distinct credential operator with private 0700 home, login shell and password enrolled by administrator, root-owned installed program and vault service. `scripts/provision_credential_desktop.sh --check|--install` verifies and stages the session entry but does not provision passwords, modify LightDM configuration or activate the marker. Dedicated seat only, no autologin, existing fixed wrapper, no TCP X11, no general Xsession grants. Existing recovery identity and provisioned configuration must be preserved. The dashboard Manage button currently displays the graphical login handoff instructions; it does NOT automatically launch or switch OS identities, and remote TLS/browser-to-local secure launch remains open. Do not put real keys into this staged qualification build. Kraken trading pair and provider tests are deferred until the independent adapter and positive permission verification under R2B; local removal is not provider revocation.
+
+## Executed qualification (2026-11-20)
+- Prior ledger snapshot archive/patch/docs checksums 4/4 PASS. Existing pinned runtime restored and dependency check clean. Seven new focused controller, real socket, private HTTP API and actual Tk widget tests PASS. Original first API fixture stopped at default test hostname, fixed to 127.0.0.1. Initial full run hit a Tk callback garbage-collection crash after GUI test; fixed window timer cleanup and same-thread test collection. Final X11 full suite 534 discovered, 532 passed, two optional skips, zero failures, exit 0 (56.810s). Node render-branch unit test PASS (no installed password inputs or save submission; development form retained); JS syntax and shell syntax PASS. Not a real Chromium browser test.
+- Fresh offline QEMU child of previous disposable R1 systemd guest, original base and parent checksums unchanged. Real named vault/gateway/backend: status-only socket accepted desk read, denied desk mutation and enrollment socket, denied gateway status access; authenticated HTTP setup reported synthetic presence without values or verification; cleanup PASS. Combined offline package index 470 entries, existing 438 package hashes PASS, APT solver and install PASS, Tk import PASS. Dedicated LightDM entry provisioned and genuine local PAM login with actual active local X11 logind session. First greeter input attempt rejected; retry passed. Initial virtual pointer input missed widgets; genuine console keyboard navigation used thereafter.
+- Actual installed masked graphical Kraken paired save, replacement (ciphertext database SHA changed), local removal and dashboard-visible status PASS. Actual separate Telegram Desk, Telegram Recovery and Grok graphical synthetic enrollment PASS. Genuine logind lock request while an unsubmitted replacement was entered closed the window/session, prior vault SHA unchanged. No provider requests, orders, real credentials or live permission. Final nine runtime/source file hashes matched guest. Scoped raw/base64/hex marker scan of nine vault/desk files and four service journals PASS; removed all remaining synthetic credentials using trusted administrative fixture. Socket retirement, clean poweroff and child disk integrity PASS. Existing source checksum manifests, test output and captured synthetic-only screenshots included in evidence. Full scope does not include actual browser persistence, live provider connectivity, TLS, remote revocation, exhaustive process/environ scan on this revision, or atomic cancellation of in-flight enrollment requests.
+
+## Disposition
+Local implementation and genuine installed graphical enrollment/status/lock scope PASS. R2A remaining: integrated one-action authenticated local handoff from Settings and actual installed browser persistence/identity and repeated cancellation/session-switch qualification (coordinate with R2C). R2B provider-specific secure adapter, Kraken distinct permissions/trading pair, Telegram identity/chat pairing and test notification, provider revocation; R2C original browser, notification/support/egress, KEK rotation and operator-reviewed recovery remain open. No GitHub changes, CI, real account credentials, desk mutation or live authorization.
